# Router Subagent Surfaces — Architecture and Design Change

Planning freeze only — do not execute WS0 or any product implementation from this document.

## How to read this document

1. **[PRD](#2-product-requirements-prd)** — what / why / who / success (minutes).
2. **[Analysis](#3-analysis)** — current system, gaps, **canonical KEEP REJECT**.
3. **[Architecture](#4-architecture)** — how the control plane, router, WBS, quality order, and evolution fit.
4. **[Design](#5-design)** — schemas, admission, workstreams WS0–WS8, **Part A then Part B** inside WS1–WS7, named tests.
5. **[Risks, rollout, and locked clarify decisions](#6-risks-rollout-and-open-decisions)** — deferred scope only; Q1–Q3 decided; KEEP REJECT stays closed except the FAST short-order amendment in KR-fast-overlay.
6. **[Appendix](#7-appendix)** — SHA lineage, matrix IDs, VAL/TST-RFL, long receipts, document integrity.

Live-spec MUST text lives only in [§2.7](#27-canonical-live-spec-must-catalog). KEEP REJECT lock text lives only in [§3.3](#33-options-considered-and-keep-reject). Pointers elsewhere are navigation, not deletions.

**OmniRoute / `/sb:agent-*` opt-in is absorbed in this freeze** (WS6 named slice + [LS-agent-pin](#ls-agent-pin); not before WS0/WS0b). Origin (provenance only — implementers do **not** need the second file): [`/Users/shafqat/.cursor/plans/omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md`](/Users/shafqat/.cursor/plans/omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md) SHA-256 `745c7f4166f70dff9181d7c8a639eb2e3519eedeb25487dda2f97e84425c2c26`. Public prefix is `/sb` (omni draft `/silver:` composed). Omni is routing-only infra, not a second public `/sb` router. Quality-order **Part A** lands before Part B consumers ([§5.2](#52-ship-sequence-ws0-ws0b-ws17-ws8-docs-release)).

## Glossary

| Term | Definition (freeze) |
|---|---|
| **Job** | User intent for **non-trivial** `/sb` work. Listed on GST-01. **FAST is not a Job.** |
| **FAST** | Same as **classified-trivial** (one concept). Required public `/sb:fast` (`WF-SILVER-FAST` / `AF-FAST-PATH`). Not a Job; not GST-01; not Evolution/`/sb:improve`. Short quality order **Executor → Verifier → Validator**. Overlay is generator-side. **Not** a legal `/sb:ladder|parallel <route>`. |
| **Wrap** | Advisor-composed wrapping user-intent Workflow (static catalog WF or composed from AFs). There is **no** `sb:agent-wrap`. |
| **Authorizer** | Admission TCB. Not Approver. Not a preference key. Hooks admit; they never invoke host `Task`. |
| **primary_checkout** | Operator primary == git main-worktree (Cursor / hosts without descendant env inheritance). Five-tool and ledger live here. |
| **extra worktree** | Overlap tree for `host_native` when Advisor touch-sets are disjoint. Omits writable ledger paths via sparse-checkout. |
| **WBS** | Job decomposition artifact (WBS-01 ASCII viz). Minted/updated only via the WBS projector. **Not** GST-01. FAST must **not** mint a Job WBS. |
| **WBS projector** | Exclusive writer `hooks/lib/wbs-projector.sh` of WBS, packet, work-spec, and plan-artifact files. |
| **nested Task** | Allowed only for descendants whose work-spec the Task-capable ancestor already persisted before this child's Task started. |
| **parent-proxy** | jsonl spawn-proxy when remaining depth is 0, host refuses nest, or a new projector write is in flight. |
| **composition Val** | Validation-loop of Advisor-composed root WF vs user intent (non-trivial). |
| **plan-time Val** | Validation-loop of Work Plan vs work-spec. |
| **Process-final Val** | Validator loop vs original user intent after top Workflow join. |
| **Q-loop** | Process re-evaluate after generated work-spec / analysis / design / plan / **code** (not docs). See LS-q-loop. |
| **GST** | Global Status team dashboard (`GST-01`, `.sb/status/STATUS-YYMMDD.md` on `origin/main`). Jobs only. |
| **PUB-01** | Authorizer-admitted catalog publish. Mid-I new catalog WF is **row 40**, not row 37. |
| **five preference keys** | Orchestrator, Advisor, Executor, Verifier, Validator. Authorizer excluded. |
| **OmniRoute** | Optional routing-only proxy (`recommended_tools.omniroute`). Not a second `/sb` router. Omni compression/memory **off** (five-tool owns those surfaces). Origin SHA `745c7f4166f70dff9181d7c8a639eb2e3519eedeb25487dda2f97e84425c2c26` (absorbed in WS6). |
| **agent_* consent** | `recommended_tools.agent_{claude,codex,cursor,opencode,pi}` Graphify-style `enabled_by_user` (`null` ask / `true` / `false`). Not role preference keys. Not Authorizer. |
| **Ladder/Parallel compose** | `/sb:ladder <route>` / `/sb:parallel <route>` run any Job catalog WF/AF (one-level XOR; not nested). Bare `/sb:ladder`/`/sb:parallel` stay standalone Jobs. `/sb:fast` is not a legal `<route>`. |
| **agent slug** | Transport-first model id: `omni/<provider>/<model>` (Omni HTTP via `scripts/agent-omni-delegate.sh`; does not require Pi), `<host>/<model>` (native `/sb:agent-<host>`), or unprefixed among **opted-in** hosts (`default_agent_host_route`). Not a public `/sb:agent-omni` command. |
| **WS0b** | Pre-implementation key spec / analysis / architecture / design matching this freeze (before WS1). Q-loop applies (analysis/design artifacts). Not runtime K/L. |
| **post-Val K/L hop** | After Process-final Val on a **Job**, Executor captures Job-scope K/L + key-doc revision (KLW-01). Runtime. Does **not** replace WS0b or docs-release. Q-loop does **not** apply (knowledge/docs/technical writing). |
| **docs-release** | Second docs pass **after WS8**. Technical writing / site-help freshness. Not WS0b; not the runtime K/L hop. |

