### 2.6 Success metrics / MVP vs post-MVP

- **MVP:** Cursor host + six-role control plane + `/sb` + Task/work-spec + WBS projector + Global Status projector (GST-01; `.sb/status/STATUS-YYMMDD.md` on `origin/main`) + overlap worktrees (`host_native` only) + Advisor-first + process-final Val + existing `sb:agent-*` rename + bootstrap migrate (ILM-01) + live E2E. Public `sb:review-fix-ladder` kept as Verifier+Process-final-Val path or thin alias until Iterate exists.
- **Post-MVP:** Iterate ladder; Levels 0–3; SB-as-parent inside Codex/Claude/OpenCode (host adapters); MIG-01 reverse-bridge / offline rollback; PROD-01 freeze/drain; full race/fault coverage including OFF/ITR/PROD matrix IDs; dedicated product-observability/SRE WF, dedicated production-rollback WF, and dedicated staging-environment WF (non-blocking — `/sb:deploy` already records monitoring links, rollback owner, and staging/preview targets; GST-01 is the Jobs dashboard, not product telemetry). See [Deferred post-MVP (non-blocking)](#deferred-post-mvp-non-blocking).
#### VAL/TST-RFL-601

- **Ship gate:** every YAML todo, WS0–WS8, and live-spec MUST maps to a named test; see LS-plan-executed-coverage and `validation-tests`. `VAL/TST-RFL-601`–`626` (including `VAL/TST-RFL-625`) remain the historical RFL coverage IDs.

- **Copies identical** after every plan edit (hashlib SHA-256).

### 2.7 Canonical live-spec MUST catalog

The following entries are the **only canonical live-spec MUST text**. Elsewhere, use the LS-* pointer. Tokens and locks below are complete (not slogans).

### LS-plan-executed-coverage

**Plan-executed test coverage (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Plan-executed test coverage (live-spec MUST):** every change this plan executes (hooks, scripts, skills, tests, docs-as-contract, projector/admission/spawn/merge/publisher, catalog, `/sb` surfaces) MUST have tests that cover **100% of those deltas** — every new/changed branch, fail-closed path, KEEP REJECT lock, and row/limb behavior this spec states.

- **100% here means coverage of plan-executed change**, not a repo-wide line-coverage mandate for unrelated files.
- Implementers MUST map each YAML todo, each Implementation workstream (WS0–WS8), and each live-spec MUST to a named test file and assertion (cite [§5.4 Named tests and coverage map](#54-named-tests-and-coverage-map) and YAML todo `validation-tests`; owners already named there and in the workstreams — `VAL/TST-RFL-601`–`626`, WS1 `tests/scripts/test-router-contract-locks.sh`, WS2 `tests/scripts/test-router-native-subagent-surfaces.sh`, WS3 admission/ingress/effects/trust plus the named primary-checkout red test, WS4 `tests/hooks/test-orchestrator-quality-loops.sh`, WS5 `tests/scripts/test-universal-silver-migrate.sh`, live E2E for the MVP slice).
- Ship is blocked until that map is complete and green.
- Unrelated existing hook tests remain optional.
- Post-MVP matrix IDs (Iterate, OFF-01, ITR-01, PROD-01, Levels 0–3, Codex/Claude/OpenCode host adapters) are not this ship’s coverage mandate.
- Do not invent a second coverage bar or new architecture rows to hold this MUST.

### LS-ship-sequence

**Ship sequence (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Ship sequence (live-spec MUST).** WS0 (repo hygiene of junk + files unused even in the **current** SB version) → WS0b (key spec / analysis / architecture / design docs matching this freeze) → WS1–WS7 product implementation → WS8 (post-implementation unnecessary-file sweep) → docs-release (second docs pass).

- **KEEP REJECT:** WS0 must not delete freeze evidence, KEEP REJECT locks, catalog/generator SOT, or tests that still gate current SB; WS0/WS0b must not implement product hooks/skills; do not start WS1 until WS0 and WS0b are done; Job post-Val Executor K/L+key-doc hop is runtime behavior, not a substitute for WS0b/WS8. **Ship sequence (live-spec MUST).** Do **not** start WS1–WS7 (or any product implementation of this freeze) until **WS0** and **WS0b** are done.
- After WS1–WS7 product implementation, **WS8** then **docs-release** MUST run.
- Numbered WS1–WS7 citations that predate this MUST still refer to those product workstreams; coverage maps use WS0–WS8.
- OmniRoute / `/sb:agent-*` Graphify-style opt-in (companion [`omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md`](/Users/shafqat/.cursor/plans/omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md) SHA-256 `745c7f4166f70dff9181d7c8a639eb2e3519eedeb25487dda2f97e84425c2c26`) is **this ship**, implemented as named slice **WS6 OmniRoute / agent-host opt-in** (after LeanCTX in `/sb:init`) plus WS2 host-surfaces / LS-agent-pin callouts and WS7 doctor/docs. It is **not** before WS0/WS0b and does **not** add a numbered workstream that breaks WS0 → WS0b → WS1–7 → WS8 → docs-release.
- **Inside WS1–WS7 (execution, not a new numbered WS):** **Part A** (quality-order core runtime) MUST land before **Part B**. Part A runs Job order **Executor → (Authorizer where required) → Verifier → Validator** and FAST short order **Executor → Verifier → Validator** (FAST is not a Job). Prerequisites: WS1 catalog/route emit and WS3 Authorizer/launch/WBS. Part B MUST **invoke** Part A — do not reimplement the role loop. Numbered WS identities stay (WS1 catalog, WS2 surfaces, WS3 Authorizer, WS4 quality-loop WS, WS5 migrate, WS6 prefs/OmniRoute routing-only, WS7 docs/Doctor/site). YAML todo order is the execution sequence. See [§5.2](#52-ship-sequence-ws0-ws0b-ws17-ws8-docs-release).

### LS-workflow-evolution

**Workflow evolution (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Workflow evolution (live-spec MUST).** Entire machinery and instructions of a workflow (Workflows / Atomic Flows / Flow Steps / Skills) MUST be evolved from the Learnings of every run to improve that **shared** workflow for **all** users — not to cater to a custom need of one user.

- **KEEP REJECT addendum:** general-improvement, not per-user customization; custom/per-user needs MUST mint a **new** workflow (`/sb:new-workflow` / WFM-01 / PUB-01 Authorizer-admitted) and use that — do **not** fork a shared catalog item in-place.
- During existing K/L capture (KLW-01 / post-Val Executor hop for non-trivial Jobs), Learnings that should enhance WF / AF / Flow Step / Skill MUST be **explicitly tagged** for future enhancement (not silent prompt drift).
- FAST is **not** subject to the Evolution mechanism or `/sb:improve`. FAST thin-capture **skips** improvement tags unless a durable learning is still captured (then that learning MAY carry a tag; applying tags still requires an `/sb:improve` Job).
- Identification happens every run; **actual edits** to installed SB artifacts happen only when the user explicitly launches `/sb:improve`.
- `/sb:improve` is **always** a **Job** (never FAST / never classified-trivial; full Job quality order + GST-01; Cursor MVP first). Empty-tag no-op MAY fail-closed as a Job with a user-visible message (not FAST, not GST skip).
- That Job applies improvement-tagged Learnings across **all** workflows that have such tags.
- Mutations MUST go through the same publisher/generator/Authorizer admission this plan already requires (PUB-01, deny-all leaves, no raw Write of ledger-omit paths; do **not** JSON-edit generated catalog).
- Subsequent `/sb` runs MUST resolve/execute the **latest evolved installed** versions of workflows / AFs / flow steps / skills (install-global `~/.silver-bullet/flows/` and project `$primary_checkout/.silver-bullet/flows/` via `hooks/lib/sb-flow-publisher.sh` as already specified — not stale packaged plugin copies when a newer evolved version exists locally).
- `/sb:init` MUST ask whether the user opts in to optional PRs of generally improved artifacts to GitHub (`alo-exp/silver-bullet`) and store that preference.
- Opt-in does **not** auto-PR every run.
- `/sb:contribute` is a separate explicit **Job** that opens a PR from locally evolved installed artifacts.
- If init opt-in is false or unset, `/sb:contribute` **fail-closes** and MUST NOT open a PR (message tells the user to opt in via `/sb:init`).
- Public routes `/sb:improve` and `/sb:contribute` only (no `/silver` dual prefix); add to generated catalog via generator.
- Catalog/skill mutations remain Authorizer-admitted; improve/contribute are **not** a new user-facing role and **not** a preference key.
- Do not move this product behavior before WS0/WS0b.

### LS-skill-extract

**Conventional-skill extract / decompose / recompose (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Conventional-skill extract / decompose / recompose (live-spec MUST).** `/sb:new-workflow` MUST accept **one or more arbitrary conventional AI skills** as input (skill file paths and/or skill directories — not only SB-native `skills/*/SKILL.md`).

- The generator MUST **analyze** those skills and **extract** the implicit workflow (the procedure the skill actually encodes) from knowledge/capability.
- It MUST **decompose** that extracted workflow into **Atomic Flows**, **compose** those AFs into a **catalog-legal Workflow**, and give each AF **Flow Steps**.
- A Flow Step **MAY attach a Skill** only when a leaf knowledge/capability packet is required.
- In SB a **Skill** is a distinct atomic packet of **knowledge or capability at the leaf** — not a jumble of implicit workflow plus knowledge in one `SKILL.md`.
- Atomic Skills MAY still carry reference files, code scripts, and other Agent Skills spec assets.
- Leaf Skills **MUST NOT** re-encode the extracted workflow.
- Convert of a conventional skill **MUST NOT** be “wrap `SKILL.md` as one `AF-EXECUTE` step.” Emitted WFs MUST stay **NW-capable / spec-compliant** (same generator bar as the rest of this `/sb:new-workflow` section).
- Synthesized AF/WF publish MUST still go through Authorizer-admitted **`PUB-01` / `hooks/lib/sb-flow-publisher.sh`** (existing PUB-01 rows; KEEP REJECT).
- Authoring-Job synthesized publish via Advisor compose + Authorizer-admitted PUB-01 is **not** Executor mid-I new catalog WF (that stays row 40).
- The authoring session remains a **Job** (Orchestrator work-spec + Advisor compose; queue-builder composition stays retired).
- `/sb:new-workflow` stays a **workflow authoring generator**; do **not** recast as Advisor-invoke-only.
- Cursor MVP first; do **not** expand host adapters.
- **Coverage MUST:** named tests/assertions for this extract/decompose/recompose path — map YAML todos `execution-registry`, `host-surfaces`, `validation-tests`, and `new-workflow-skill-extract` / WS1+WS2 / this MUST / `VAL/TST-RFL-625` / WFM-01 (golden fixture: conventional skill in → catalog-legal WF of AFs with Flow Steps and leaf Skills only where needed; negative: wrap-as-one-AF-EXECUTE is fail-closed).
- Do not mark YAML todos completed — implementation is later.

### LS-q-loop

**Q-loop (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Q-loop (live-spec MUST).** After any **generated** work spec, analysis, design, plan, or **code** artifact — and **not** after documentation or technical writing — Process MUST run a **Q-loop**: evaluate the artifact against Silver Bullet’s nine Design Quality Gates in skill order (`modularity`, `reusability`, `scalability`, `security`, `reliability`, `usability`, `testability`, `extensibility`, and `ai-llm-safety` when the artifact includes AI/LLM behavior).

- If any applicable gate is unsatisfied, the **generating** role (the role that produced that artifact) MUST address the findings and the Q-loop MUST re-run on the revised artifact until all applicable gates pass or the hop fail-closes (`blocked_q_loop` or the existing fail-closed row that owns that hop — do not invent a silent skip).
- Q-loop **check** (the gate evaluation, not the fix) MUST use the same `{ runtime, model, effort }` as **Advisor** by default, including the Board Consolidator identity when Advisor is multi-model Parallel.
- During `/sb:init` (or later init if prefs are missing) the user MAY assign a distinct Q-loop checker tuple; that override is a preference entry, **not** a sixth user-facing role and **not** an Authorizer key.
- Authorizer remains hook/admission TCB. FAST / classified-trivial / `/sb:fast` MUST skip Q-loop (Q-loop is Job generated-artifact machinery; FAST short order is Executor → Verifier → Validator only).
- Cursor MVP first; do not expand host adapters for Q-loop.

### LS-unified-review

**Unified code review / thermos absorb (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Unified code review / thermos absorb (live-spec MUST).** After Advisor is **satisfied** with Executor-generated **code** (A-loop two-clean on that product; not on docs/technical writing), Process MUST run **one** SB code-review workflow — the existing SB review mechanism (`sb:review` / review-request / review / review-triage contracts, public `/sb` ids) **enhanced by** Cursor `/thermos` instructions.

- That unified workflow MUST (1) run the thermo-nuclear **correctness** pass (bugs, breakages, security, devex regressions, feature-flag leaks — `thermo-nuclear-review`) and the thermo-nuclear **code-quality** pass (maintainability, structure, file-size growth, spaghetti, abstractions — `thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review`) **in parallel**, (2) **synthesize** those two reports (overlapping findings weigh more; the review-role model resolves disagreements), and (3) **not** also invoke Cursor `/thermos` as a separate command, and **not** run a third overlapping security/correctness pass over the same diff (fold thermos correctness into this review; keep Authorizer/TCB and secret-scan paths that are not diff-review).
- Code review MUST use the Advisor `{ runtime, model, effort }` (or Board Consolidator identity) by default unless the user assigns a distinct code-review tuple at preference input — again **not** a new user-facing role key and **not** Authorizer.
- Findings that are not wrong MUST be APPLY-ACCEPT-complete; the **preceding** role (**Executor**) fixes.
- Do not reopen KEEP REJECT.
- Cursor MVP first.

### LS-ladder-parallel

**Generalized multi-model roles — Ladder and Parallel (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Generalized multi-model roles — Ladder and Parallel (live-spec MUST).** For **any** quality-order LLM role (Orchestrator, Advisor, Executor, Verifier, Validator) the user MAY specify **multiple** `{ runtime, model, effort }` members.

- **Authorizer is not a preference key** and MUST NOT become a multi-model Board (KEEP REJECT).
- **Ladder** and **Parallel** are first-class **workflow patterns**, not quality-order-only modes.
- The user MAY invoke them **directly** as public **`/sb:ladder`** and **`/sb:parallel`** (independent Jobs: Orchestrator work-spec + Advisor compose; catalog ids may remain `WF-SILVER-*`; public ids `sb` / `sb:` / `/sb` only — no dual `/silver` window).
- Inside quality-order, if the user specifies no mode, **Ladder is the default**.
- The user MAY override the mode **per task**.
- **Ladder:** members run **one after another on the same artifact**.
- `/sb:ladder` absorbs today’s `/silver:review-fix-ladder`, preserving **100%** of current RFL instructions and code (Policy A/B/C, APPLY ACCEPT completeness, rungs review-only).
- SB MUST order rungs **least capable → most capable** even if the user listed another order (in-repo slug catalog / ranking already used by RFL; do not invent OpenCode Max; Fast remains forbidden unless the user explicitly says Fast).
- When a Ladder is **inside** the quality-order, the **preceding** role executes the fix step after each rung: Executor fixes when an Advisor Ladder reviews Executor work; Advisor fixes when a Validator Ladder reviews Advisor work; similarly for other adjacent hops.
- Standalone `/sb:ladder` keeps launcher APPLY ACCEPT (100% RFL).
- **Parallel:** all specified member tuples launch together; a **Consolidator** coordinates, collects review feedback, de-duplicates, and **is the final role-player** for that hop (generalize today’s Authorizer-admitted `advisor_board_unify` deny-all unifier; Board of one still launches the unifier).
- Unresolved Parallel conflict fail-closes as `blocked_plan_of_action_review` (existing row 6), not a new silent merge.
- Standalone `/sb:parallel` is the same pattern as a Job: Consolidator reviews/unifies only (does not implement product fixes); APPLY ACCEPT of the synthesized set is the Job launcher unless a generating role is already in-session.
- Coverage MUST name `tests/scripts/test-sb-parallel.sh` (create it) alongside `tests/scripts/test-sb-ladder.sh` and `tests/scripts/test-sb-ladder-parallel-compose.sh` (create at execute).

#### Job-route compose (any catalog WF/AF)

- **Any** Job catalog WF/AF (including `/sb:clarify` / `AF-CLARIFY`, spec, plan, execute, review, deep-research, feature, bugfix, …) MAY run in **Ladder mode or Parallel mode** as a first-class compose. This is not only the six-role quality-order overlay and not only bare `/sb:ladder` as a standalone review-like Job with no inner WF.
- **Locked public grammar (Cursor MVP):** `/sb:ladder <route>` and `/sb:parallel <route>` where `<route>` is a catalog Job route (`clarify`, `sb:clarify`, or `/sb:clarify`). Examples: `/sb:ladder clarify`, `/sb:parallel clarify`. Do **not** offer three equivalent CLIs. Do **not** add a second public `/sb:clarify-ladder` (etc.) route per WF — compose is **one** ladder/parallel WF wrapping the named inner route.
- Bare `/sb:clarify` stays the **non-composed** Job AF (quality-order still applies; Advisor board may still exist). Explicit `/sb:ladder|parallel clarify` **is** the multi-model independent (Parallel) or sequential capability-order (Ladder) run of **that** workflow.
- Bare `/sb:ladder` / `/sb:parallel` without `<route>` remain the standalone Jobs already specified (RFL absorb / Parallel consolidator Job).
- **Parallel compose:** members `{ runtime, model, effort }` (and optional agent pin) each run the **same** inner WF/AF **independently**; Consolidator unifies; unresolved conflict → `blocked_plan_of_action_review`. Not last-write-wins. Consolidator remains review-only (does not implement product fixes).
- **Ladder compose:** same inner WF/AF, least-capable → most-capable. Standalone compose: launcher APPLY ACCEPT. If already inside a Job quality-order, preceding role fixes as already specified.
- Authorizer is still not a member. Inner WF still Authorizer-admitted launches.
- Inner WF still gets WBS/packets via projector when it is a Job (clarify as a hop inside a parent Job vs clarify as wrapping Job — both must work). If `/sb:ladder clarify` is itself a Job, it has GST/WBS per Job rules; inner clarify is the composed work.
- **FAST:** `/sb:fast` is **not** a legal `<route>` (fail-closed). Clarify is a Job AF — legal.
- **One-level compose:** ladder XOR parallel; nested `/sb:ladder /sb:parallel <route>` (or the reverse) **fail-closes**. Do not invent `/sb:multi-ai-task`.
- **WS1** emit: no extra public routes (argument on existing `/sb:ladder` / `/sb:parallel`). **WS4** Jobs runtime. **WS7** docs.
- Cursor MVP first.

### LS-retire-multi-ai

**Retire `/silver:multi-ai-task` with no transition (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Retire `/silver:multi-ai-task` with no transition (live-spec MUST).** Public `/silver:multi-ai-task` (catalog `AF-MULTI-AI-TASK` / wrapping WF / plugin command / `skills/silver-multi-ai-task/` / `templates/orchestrator-workers/MULTI-AI-TASK.md`) is **removed in this ship** — no deprecation window, no `/sb:multi-ai-task` alias, no dual `/silver` shim.

- `/sb:ladder` and `/sb:parallel` replace it: they already launch native or `/sb:agent-*` members and their models.
- **Absorb, then delete:** host-matrix fail-closed-before-dispatch (`SB_MULTI_AI_UNSUPPORTED_HOST` and `reference/host-matrix-v1.json`) into Ladder/Parallel host admission; model-family registry (`reference/model-family-registry-v1.json`) into least-capable→most-capable Ladder ordering and Parallel member identity; pool algebra / budget defaults only where the user did **not** already specify explicit member tuples (explicit `{ runtime, model, effort, optional agent pin }` wins); `--output-root` / contribution artifacts / consolidator spine into `/sb:parallel` Consolidator receipts (Authorizer-admitted unifier); sequential multi-model passes into `/sb:ladder` (do **not** fork a second RFL).
- Do **not** keep `AF-MULTI-AI-TASK.execution.worker_template` pointed at `MULTI-AI-TASK.md` — retarget generator source so regen emits no public multi-ai-task route and no that worker template.
- Named tests must **fail** if `silver-multi-ai-task` / `/silver:multi-ai-task` / `/sb:multi-ai-task` still appear as public routes after regen.
- Target architecture for deep research is **`WF-DEEP-RESEARCH`** (fresh Job re-implementation, public `/sb:deep-research`, full Job quality order) — **not** `AF-MULTI-AI-TASK` and **not** `/sb:multi-ai-task`. Current `silver:deep-research-multi-ai` / `WF-SILVER-DEEP-RESEARCH-MULTI-AI` is **deprecated until retired** as public `/sb:legacy-dr` (not an alias of `/sb:multi-ai-task`). See [LS-deep-research](#ls-deep-research).
- Cursor MVP first.
- Do not JSON-edit catalog; generator then regen.

### LS-post-val-kl

**Post-Val K/L capture and key-doc revision (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Post-Val K/L capture and key-doc revision (live-spec MUST).** Against **user intent**, the **final** quality-order step of the Job is the Validator **Process-final validation-loop** (VALP-01).

- After that loop **passes**, Process MUST run a **post-Val capture hop**: (1) capture knowledge/learnings from the **entire task** through this plan’s existing K/L mechanism (AM opted in → `memory_save` then classify/promote; AM not opted in → `kl_write_am_skipped`; durable promote AM → K/L; `kl_post_write_no_insights` when there is nothing to promote; no raw Write of `docs/knowledge/` / `docs/learnings/` — named helpers only; KLW-01), **and** (2) check whether any **key project doc** needs update/revision (the doc-scheme / `/sb:ensure-docs` canonical set already in-repo — README, ARCHITECTURE, TESTING, CHANGELOG, and other governed docs as applicable) and land those revisions when needed.
- **Both (1) and (2) are Executor work** (Executor `{ runtime, model, effort }`, including `/sb:agent-*` pin if set) — **not** the Advisor `knowledge_postwrite` leaf as the producer.
- That Executor product is then **reviewed by Advisor** and **verified by Verifier** (ordinary A then V on this hop; Q-loop does **not** apply because these artifacts are knowledge/docs/technical writing; unified thermos code-review does **not** apply unless the hop also emitted code).
- Findings that are not wrong are APPLY-ACCEPT-complete; Executor fixes.
- Do **not** run a second Process-final Val against original user intent on this hop — Val vs user intent already passed.
- Unresolved A/V on the capture hop fail-closes on the existing A/V rows, not by skipping K/L.
- **FAST / classified-trivial / `/sb:fast`** keeps the existing FAST thin-capture path only (not this Job post-Val hop; FAST is not a Job and skips Process-final-Val-as-Job; FAST still runs short-order Validator before thin capture).
- Cursor MVP first.

### LS-fast-short-order

**FAST short quality order (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**FAST short quality order (live-spec MUST).** **FAST** and **classified-trivial** are the **same** concept (unify terminology; do not keep two products). FAST is **required**. Public user-facing command is **`/sb:fast`** (catalog `sb:fast` / `WF-SILVER-FAST` / `AF-FAST-PATH`; generator-side overlay; do not JSON-edit those records).

- FAST is **not** a Job and **must not** appear on GST-01 (no `original_intent_hash` Job mint; no GST projector write). FAST **must not** mint a Job WBS (thin-capture / thin wrap path is not a Job WBS).
- FAST is **not** subject to Evolution or `/sb:improve`.
- FAST **must** run the **short quality order Executor → Verifier → Validator** (not the six-role Job order; **not** skip-all-quality). FAST Validator is a short-order hop on the FAST leaf product — **not** composition-Val and **not** Process-final-Val-as-Job.
- FAST **still skips:** Job GST; Advisor-first planning / Advisor compose; Board of Advisors; composition-Val; plan-time Validation-loop; A-loop Mentorship; Process-final-Val-as-Job (including Process-synthesis I and Process-scope A/V); Job post-Val K/L hop; Q-loop; unified thermos code-review; Evolution/`/sb:improve`; Authorizer-as-quality-order-role (Authorizer remains TCB admission of FAST launches).
- Orchestrator classifies and catalog-dispatches `AF-FAST-PATH` (not WF mint). parent≠implementer. Live composition remains **`AF-FAST-PATH` only**; catalog extra AFs (`AF-PLAN`, `AF-VALIDATE`, `AF-VERIFY`, `AF-QUALITY-GATE`, `AF-EXECUTE`) **must not run**.
- After short-order Validator passes, FAST thin capture still runs (AM opted in → `memory_save` then classify/promote; AM not opted in → `kl_write_am_skipped`). Thin-capture deny-all is not a second Job.
- Durable-edit misclassify fail-closed reclassifies into the Advisor-composed Job path (that work **is** a Job and **does** hit GST).
- Named execute-time test: `tests/scripts/test-sb-fast.sh`. WS4 owns short-order runtime; WS1 emits the public route; WS7 documents it.
- Cursor MVP first.

### LS-deep-research

**Deep research Job re-implementation (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Deep research Job re-implementation (live-spec MUST).** `WF-SILVER-DEEP-RESEARCH-MULTI-AI` becomes **`WF-DEEP-RESEARCH`**, freshly re-implemented under the **new** workflow mechanisms including **full Job quality order** (work-spec + Advisor compose + composition-Val + plan-time Val + I/A/Verification + Process-final Val + post-Val K/L). Public user-facing command is **`/sb:deep-research`**.

- Do **not** leave deep-research bound to `AF-MULTI-AI-TASK` as the target architecture.
- Current implementation is **deprecated until retired**, available as **`/sb:legacy-dr`** (not `/sb:multi-ai-task`, not `/silver:multi-ai-task`).
- Public `/silver:multi-ai-task` / `/sb:multi-ai-task` stay **retired with no alias** ([LS-retire-multi-ai](#ls-retire-multi-ai)).
- Catalog emit is generated (no JSON-edit). WS1 emits `/sb:deep-research` and `/sb:legacy-dr`; WS4 owns `WF-DEEP-RESEARCH` Job runtime; WS7 docs/Doctor/site; WS8 retires leftover current-impl surfaces when the deprecation window ends.
- Named execute-time tests: `tests/scripts/test-sb-deep-research.sh`, `tests/scripts/test-sb-legacy-dr.sh`.
- Cursor MVP first.

### LS-agent-pin

**Per-member `/sb:agent-*` pin (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Per-member `/sb:agent-*` pin (live-spec MUST).** When the user specifies models (init prefs, later prefs, or per-task), they MAY also specify that a given member MUST run **only** through a named external SB agent: `/sb:agent-cursor` | `/sb:agent-codex` | `/sb:agent-claude` | `/sb:agent-opencode` | `/sb:agent-pi` (and `/sb:agent-goose` / `/sb:agent-hermes` when those skills exist), or `host_native`.

- That pin is an extra field on the member tuple, **not** a new user-facing role and **not** an Authorizer key.
- Cold `/sb:agent-*` still dispatches the **shipped** `WF-AGENT-DELEGATE-ENTRY` / `AF-AGENT-DELEGATE` / `nested_executor` leaves — **MUST NOT** add `sb:agent-wrap` or a second catalog WF (KEEP REJECT).
- **Duty parity:** whatever duties a **host-native** subagent has under this spec (receipts, envelope/work-spec, projector-only WBS via the Task-capable ancestor, spawn-proxy jsonl, `remaining_depth`, five-tool at `$primary_checkout`, deny-all leaves, no raw Edit of ledger-omit paths) MUST apply to the **external** agent as well.
- Because an external agent is always launched **through** a host-native subagent, that host-native wrapper MUST **ensure** the external agent actually performs those duties (it is the compliance envelope: it stamps/relays receipts, refuses non-compliant writes, parent-proxies when the host cannot nest, and fail-closes rather than silently dropping SB requirements).
- HINST-01 still: instruction-only hosts have no PreToolUse/PostToolUse — Authorizer-bound expected writes reconcile via parent-proxy after the fact.
- Cursor MVP first; Codex/Claude/OpenCode/Pi adapters remain post-MVP except as already specified for `/sb:agent-*` leaves.
- **Same ship (absorbed omni; origin SHA `745c7f4166f70dff9181d7c8a639eb2e3519eedeb25487dda2f97e84425c2c26`):** pin field stays `host_native` | `/sb:agent-{cursor,codex,claude,opencode,pi}`. `omni/<provider>/<model>` is **slug transport** (thin `scripts/agent-omni-delegate.sh`; does **not** require Pi; **no** public `/sb:agent-omni`; **no** `sb:agent-wrap`). Launch fail-closes / skill refuses if the matching `recommended_tools.agent_*` or `omniroute` (for `omni/` slugs) is opted out. Unprefixed models use `default_agent_host_route` among opted-in hosts only. Dual-mode `--interaction-mode` unchanged.

### LS-autonomous-e2e-order

**Canonical autonomous E2E utilization order (live-spec MUST)** — canonical.

**Canonical autonomous E2E utilization order (live-spec MUST).** When autonomous mode is given a **vague app idea** through **deployment tested and operational**, Orchestrator MUST utilize catalog Workflows / Atomic Flows plus **one** Process quality-order overlay in the **runtime order** below. Public names are `/sb:…` (compose `/silver:` as `/sb:`). Do **not** add a second Process. Do **not** make FAST a Job. Do **not** mint a Job WBS on FAST. Job WBS (decomposition) and GST-01 (team dashboard) are both named — do not conflate. Do **not** JSON-edit the catalog; generator emit already covers these routes.

AGENTS.md / Help Center **presentation** SDLC order (entry/router → discovery → primary delivery → fast/specialized → infrastructure → ship → post-delivery gates → operations) is **documentation listing**, not this runtime utilization order.

#### Spine (vague idea → live operational)

Process quality-order hops are marked **Process** (not an AF). Catalog WF/AF hops are marked **WF** / **AF**.

1. `/sb:init` — when the repo is not SB-initialized (prefs + optional contribute + Omni/`agent_*` consent). **Not a Job.** Role: installer/Orchestrator setup. Catalog: Process setup (not an AF).
2. `/sb:doctor` — when install/runtime is unverified or drifting. **Not a Job.** Role: inspect/`--fix`. Catalog: Process setup.
3. `/sb:migrate` — when legacy `silver` state remains. Bootstrap TCB / in-product route. Catalog: Process setup.
4. `/sb` (`WF-SILVER-ROUTER` / `AF-ROUTE`) — classify trivial vs Job. **Job vs FAST** decided here. Role: Orchestrator.

5. **FAST branch (not the Job spine):** if classified-trivial, catalog-dispatch `/sb:fast` / `AF-FAST-PATH` **only**. Short quality order **Executor → Verifier → Validator**, then FAST thin-capture. **Not a Job.** No GST. **No Job WBS** (FAST must not mint a Job WBS / GST Job row; thin-capture / thin wrap path is not a Job WBS). Catalog extra AFs (`AF-PLAN`, `AF-VALIDATE`, `AF-VERIFY`, `AF-QUALITY-GATE`, `AF-EXECUTE`) **must not run**. Durable-edit misclassify fail-closes into step 6.

6. **Job wrap (Process, not an AF):** Orchestrator work-spec + GST-01; Advisor compose wrapping Workflow; composition-Val until `comp_val_verified`; Job K/L pre-read. Role: Orchestrator / Advisor / Validator. For a vague app idea the default wrapping WF is `/sb:feature` (`WF-SILVER-FEATURE`). **WBS creation is the next numbered hop (step 7)** — same Process-resolve WBS as §4.3, not a second mint.
7. **Job WBS mint / live packets (Process, not an AF):** After work-spec exists and Advisor has composed the wrapping WF (step 6), Orchestrator invokes `hooks/lib/wbs-projector.sh` as the **only** writer of WBS, packets, work-spec, and plan artifacts (`primary_checkout` sole write root). This is the **same** Job WBS §4.3 creates from user intent at Process resolve; composition-Val remint may rewrite it **before** Executor I — **do not invent a second WBS**. Packet mint and live WBS updates continue as AFs/NWs are scheduled (DFS / two-limb KEEP REJECT unchanged). **GST-01** is the team Jobs dashboard; **WBS** is the Job decomposition artifact — do not conflate. Role: Orchestrator (projector). Executor I still starts only after `plan_val_verified`.
8. `/sb:context` / `AF-ORIENT` (brownfield also `/sb:scan`). **Job** (inside wrapping WF). Role: Executor under composed plan. **AF.**
9. `/sb:clarify` / `AF-CLARIFY` — vague idea → decision-ready brief. **Job.** **AF.**
10. Research insert when stack/architecture/API is unknown: `/sb:deep-research` (`WF-DEEP-RESEARCH`, full Job quality order). `/sb:legacy-dr` only until retired. **Never** `/sb:multi-ai-task`. **Job.** **WF.** Maps onto `AF-DECIDE` in the feature tree.
11. `/sb:spec` / `AF-SPECIFY`. **Job.** **AF.**
12. `AF-QUALITY-GATE` pre-plan (`/sb:quality-gates`). **Job.** **AF.**
13. `/sb:plan` / `AF-PLAN`. **Job.** **AF.**
14. UI scope: `/sb:ui-contract` / `AF-DESIGN-CONTRACT`. **Job.** **AF.**
15. **Q-loop** (nine Design Quality Gates) after generated work-spec / analysis / design / plan (and later code). **Process** (not an AF). Generating role fixes; checker defaults to Advisor tuple.
16. **Plan-time Val** until `plan_val_verified`. **Process.** Role: Validator (deny-all leaf).
17. `/sb:execute` / `AF-EXECUTE` — I-loop. **Job.** **AF.** Role: Executor. Then **A-loop** (Advisor) then **Verification-loop** (Verifier) — **Process** overlay on the AF, not extra AFs. Packet mint / live WBS updates continue as AFs are scheduled (same projector; not a second WBS).
18. Coverage gaps: `/sb:test` (`WF-SILVER-TEST`). Failures: `/sb:debug` / `AF-DEBUG`. **Job.** **WF/AF.**
19. UI scope: `/sb:ui-review` / `AF-UI-QUALITY`. **Job.** **AF.**
20. **Unified thermos review** after A-clean Executor **code** (LS-unified-review). **Process** (not an AF). Default Advisor tuple; Executor fixes APPLY-ACCEPT findings.
21. `WF-POST-EXEC-GATES`: `/sb:review-request` → `/sb:review` → `/sb:triage` (`AF-REVIEW-REQUEST` / `AF-REVIEW` / `AF-REVIEW-TRIAGE`) → `/sb:verify` + `verify-tests` + UAT evidence (`AF-VERIFY`) → `/sb:secure` (`AF-SECURE`) → optional `/sb:validate` (`AF-VALIDATE`) → pre-ship `AF-QUALITY-GATE` → `/sb:branch-finish` / `/sb:completion-audit` / `/sb:ship`. **Job.** **WF/AF.**
22. **Process-synthesis + Process-scope A/V** then **Process-final Val** vs original user intent. **Process** (not an AF; not a second Process). Role: Validator at roll-up.
23. **Post-Val K/L + key docs** (KLW-01; `/sb:ensure-docs` / `AF-DOCUMENT` as needed). **Process** plus **AF** for docs. Role: Executor produces; Advisor reviews; Verifier verifies. No second Process-final Val on this hop.
24. `/sb:release` (`WF-SILVER-RELEASE`) — milestone UAT audit, ship, `/sb:create-release`, CI green. **Job.** **WF.**
25. `/sb:deploy` (`WF-SILVER-DEPLOY`) — prefer dry-run / preview / **staging** before production; record health, monitoring links, **rollback** command/owner. **Job.** **WF.**
26. Production traffic: `/sb:canary` (`WF-SILVER-CANARY`). **Job.** **WF.**
27. **Ops:** GST-01 (Jobs dashboard, not a WF; not the WBS); `/sb:doctor` on drift; `/sb:incident` (`WF-SILVER-INCIDENT`) on production failure; `/sb:forensics` / `/sb:retro` as needed. Incident is a **Job.** Doctor/GST are **not** Jobs.
28. Evolution (not every ship): `/sb:improve` **always a Job**; `/sb:contribute` Job if init opt-in else fail-closed. **WF** via LS-workflow-evolution.
29. OmniRoute / `/sb:agent-*` — **opt-in nested_executor leaves** on any Job hop (absorbed omni). Not a spine step; not `/sb:agent-omni`; not `sb:agent-wrap`.

#### Branches (replace wrapping WF at step 6; do not dump 80 skills)

- **Bugfix:** `/sb:bugfix` (`WF-SILVER-BUGFIX`: orient → debug → plan → execute → post-exec gates).
- **UI-primary:** `/sb:ui` (`WF-SILVER-UI`: same as feature with mandatory design contract + UI quality).
- **DevOps / infra:** `/sb:devops` (`WF-SILVER-DEVOPS`: blast-radius → devops-route → gates → secure → orient → plan → validate → execute → post-exec).
- **Research-only:** `/sb:deep-research` as the wrapping Job (not a feature subtree insert).
- **New-workflow authoring:** `/sb:new-workflow` (authoring Job; generator; not Advisor-invoke-only).
- **Ladder / Parallel:** `/sb:ladder` / `/sb:parallel` as first-class Jobs, as quality-order modes (Ladder default inside quality-order), **and** as **mode compose on any Job route** (example: `/sb:parallel clarify`). Not only “replace wrapping WF.” `/sb:fast` is not a legal compose `<route>`.
- **Specialized:** `/sb:content`, `/sb:refactor`, `/sb:benchmark`, `/sb:compare`, `/sb:ingest` — Advisor-composed when intent matches; not the greenfield spine.
- **FAST:** step 5 only (no Job WBS). **Improve/contribute:** step 28 only.

#### This-ship completeness

Catalog already contains discovery, work-spec (Process), research, UX, security, test/UAT, staging-as-deploy-target, deploy, rollback-readiness, canary, incident, doctor, GST, WBS (Job decomposition; projector-only). No new public `/sb` route and no new AF/WF this ship. Named test: `tests/scripts/test-sb-autonomous-e2e-order.sh` (must assert Job WBS mint is numbered spine hop 7; FAST has no Job WBS; VAL/TST-RFL-617 family). **WS4** runtime (Advisor compose + Job quality-order follows this spine for vague-to-operational intent; ladder/parallel compose is `/sb:ladder|parallel <route>` on existing Jobs). **WS7** documents runtime vs presentation. **WS1** emit unchanged (no per-WF `/sb:*-ladder` routes; `<route>` is an argument on existing `/sb:ladder` / `/sb:parallel`).

## 3. Analysis

### 3.1 Current system

The parent orchestrator session is spawn-only.

- Skills and commands are `silver:*`.
- Hidden adapter runners and `silver:agent-*` CLI/TUI skills already exist for Codex, Claude, Cursor, Pi, and OpenCode.
- Hooks and scripts are automatic shell programs on tool use; they cannot invoke Cursor `Task`.
- Live parent-guard tests treat parent implementation as forbidden and must be rewritten so the allowlisted projector may write WBS/packet paths under `$primary_checkout/.planning/`, `hooks/lib/sb-spawn-proxy.sh` may append and CAS-consume exactly `$primary_checkout/.planning/sb-spawn-proxy.jsonl`, and the merge helper may write worktree code paths, while Orchestrator still must not implement product code or raw-Edit the jsonl.
- Both helpers take `primary_checkout` as the sole write root and fail-closed unless the write-root argument equals `$SB_PRIMARY_CHECKOUT` (process env `$SB_PRIMARY_CHECKOUT` when set is the primary even when it is not git's main worktree; git main-worktree is fallback only when env is unset); they do not trust the LLM envelope path alone.

There is no Authorizer/Verifier privilege split, no Advisor-owned plan handoff, no Process-final Validator role, and no central live WBS with callback-only child reports.

- Control-plane state is scattered across host-specific directories. [`docs/RUNTIME-COMPATIBILITY.md`](docs/RUNTIME-COMPATIBILITY.md) currently says Silver Bullet does not route models; this architecture supersedes that sentence for **role launches**.
- The Orchestrator **session** model remains the host UI’s choice.

### 3.2 Gaps this freeze closes

The current spawn-only parent, dual `silver:*` surfaces, missing Authorizer/Verifier split, missing Advisor-owned plan handoff, missing Process-final Validator, and missing live WBS are the gaps named in Current system. This freeze closes them with the architecture below. This freeze also closes the gap that `/sb:agent-*` hosts and optional OmniRoute lack Graphify-style `recommended_tools` consent, transport-first slugs, init after LeanCTX, and doctor `--fix` (companion [`omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md`](/Users/shafqat/.cursor/plans/omni_agent_opt-in_67f2f73a.plan.md) SHA-256 `745c7f4166f70dff9181d7c8a639eb2e3519eedeb25487dda2f97e84425c2c26`; composed under existing `/sb:agent-*` / five-tool / init — not a second control plane). Rejected alternatives are **only** in §3.3 — do not reopen them in §6.

### 3.3 Options considered and KEEP REJECT

This section is the **only canonical KEEP REJECT catalog**. Do **not** reopen these as open decisions. Elsewhere, use the KR-* pointer.

Every KEEP REJECT lock from the freeze is listed in full below (changelog “KEEP REJECT intact” round receipts live in [Appendix A](#a-sha-lineage-and-round-receipts), not here).

### KR-catalog-generated

KEEP REJECT — complete `sb:<route>` catalog is **generated** from APO (`scripts/generate-apo-catalog.py` and named builders). Do **not** JSON-edit generated `docs/apo-catalog.json` as SOT. Mutations go through generator source then regen. Synthesized AF/WF publish still goes through Authorizer-admitted **PUB-01** / `hooks/lib/sb-flow-publisher.sh`.

### KR-fast-overlay

KEEP REJECT — FAST overlay is **generator-side** (FAST = classified-trivial). Generated denies/composition must **not** re-impose the **six-role Job** gates on `/sb:fast`. FAST **does** run Executor → Verifier → Validator (short order). Do **not** JSON-edit `AF-FAST-PATH` / `WF-SILVER-FAST`. **FAST is not a Job** and must not appear on GST-01. FAST is not Evolution/`/sb:improve`. This amendment is the locked Q1 clarify; do not reopen other KEEP REJECT items.

### KR-evolution-not-custom

KEEP REJECT addendum — general-improvement of the shared catalog for **all** users, not per-user customization. Custom/per-user needs MUST mint a **new** workflow (`/sb:new-workflow` / WFM-01 / PUB-01 Authorizer-admitted) and use that — do **not** fork a shared catalog item in-place.

### KR-projector-exclusive

KEEP REJECT — exclusive WBS/packet/work-spec/plan writer is `hooks/lib/wbs-projector.sh`. Admission **requests** the projector; it is not a second packet writer. Spawn-proxy jsonl is not a packet file (`hooks/lib/sb-spawn-proxy.sh`). DFS **tri-color** cycle detection (visited-set alone is not sufficient). Two-limb in-plan Executor mint only (Work Plan–cited WF/AF **or** a pre-existing catalog WF that supports that cited node).

### KR-off-01-post-mvp

KEEP REJECT — OFF-01 (and Iterate / ITR-01 / PROD-01 freeze/drain / Levels 0–3 / Codex/Claude/OpenCode host adapters as Orchestrator parent) stay **post-MVP**. MVP workstream acceptance must not require those matrix IDs.

### KR-l598-no-abandon

KEEP REJECT — L598: no abandonment-by-silence. Timeout/disconnect/missing process/lease silence cannot prove abandonment and cannot prove row-1 limb (b). Catalog/lock already lock-only — no schema change to add `nested_executor` as a catalog JSON field (`additionalProperties: false` unchanged).

### KR-coverage-plan-executed

KEEP REJECT — 100% means coverage of **plan-executed change**, not repo-wide line coverage of unrelated files. Map each YAML todo, each WS0–WS8, and each live-spec MUST to a named test file/assertion (`VAL/TST-RFL-601`–`626` and named WS tests). Ship is blocked until that map is complete and green. Post-MVP matrix IDs stay out of this ship's coverage mandate. Canonical map: [Appendix B](#b-yaml-todo-test-ws-map) and [§5.4](#54-named-tests-and-coverage-map).

### KR-ws0-preserve-evidence

KEEP REJECT — WS0 must **not** delete freeze evidence, KEEP REJECT locks, frozen RFL evidence under `.planning/rfl-router-subagent-surfaces-*`, catalog/generator SOT, or tests that still gate current SB. WS0/WS0b must not implement product hooks/skills. Do not start WS1 until WS0 and WS0b are done. Job post-Val Executor K/L+key-doc hop is **runtime** behavior, not a substitute for WS0b / WS8 / docs-release.

### KR-contribute-fail-closed

KEEP REJECT — `/sb:init` stores optional GitHub PR opt-in. `/sb:contribute` is an explicit Job to `alo-exp/silver-bullet` and **fail-closes** if opted out or unset. Opt-in does **not** auto-PR.

### KR-no-dual-silver

KEEP REJECT — public prefix is `/sb` / `sb:` / `sb` only. **No dual `/silver` window.** Historical `silver:` cutover is `bash scripts/sb-migrate-from-silver.sh` (and plugin postinstall), not only `/sb:migrate`.

### KR-row-40

KEEP REJECT — mid-I **new PUB-01 definition / new catalog WF record** is `blocked_executor_wf_out_of_plan` (**row 40**), not row 37. Composition remint / row-40 Advisor re-compose **mints a new `launch_id`**. Authoring-Job synthesized publish via Advisor compose + Authorizer-admitted PUB-01 is **not** Executor mid-I new catalog WF.

### KR-authorizer-not-pref

KEEP REJECT — Authorizer is admission TCB: **not** Approver, **not** a user-facing preference key, **not** a multi-model Board. ESC-02 has **no A**. Hooks admit; they never invoke host `Task`.

